# Line endings are decided here, not by each machine's git config.
#
# Without this file, `core.autocrlf=true` (the Windows default, and what is set
# on at least one machine that touches this repository) rewrites every text file
# to CRLF on checkout. Prettier's `endOfLine` default is `lf`, so `npm run
# format` -- the exact command CI runs -- fails on a fresh clone before a single
# edit is made. Reproduced: `git checkout` a source file, and it comes back with
# CRLF terminators and immediately fails the format gate.
#
# `eol=lf` pins the working tree as well as the repository, so the result no
# longer depends on who cloned it or how their git is configured.
* text=auto eol=lf

# Binary, so git must never touch the bytes.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.ico binary
*.webp binary
*.pdf binary
*.jks binary
*.keystore binary
*.woff binary
*.woff2 binary
